<title>FRANCE: ADP-New York top originating gateway Jan-Feb 97.</title>
<headline>ADP-New York top originating gateway Jan-Feb 97.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top airport gateway for imports to Charles de Gaulle and Orly airports in the first two months of 1997.</p>
<p>The top ten orignating airport gateways for ADP imports in January-February 1997, with the percentage change on the same period in 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>			  Jan-Feb  pct change</p>
<p> 1  New York	   5,465   down  9.3pct</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	    4,453   down  1.3</p>
<p> 3  Tokyo		3,361   up   60.3</p>
<p> 4  Hong Kong	  2,713   down  4.8</p>
<p> 5  Montreal	   2,670   down  7.6</p>
<p> 6  Los Angeles	2,200   down 18.8</p>
<p> 7  Singapore	  1,352   up   64.2</p>
<p> 8  Casablanca	 1,117   down 34.2</p>
<p> 9  Miami		1,082   down  7.7</p>
<p> 10 Seoul		1,081   up   48.5</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
